  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The proposed comparisons omit a residual-only variant using baseline BCE. A four-way comparison—baseline, objective-only, residual-only, combined—is needed to distinguish architectural gains from loss changes.",
    "A sigmoid bounds the gate but does not bound the residual contribution: item-embedding norms may grow relative to normalized SASRec states. Specify representation scaling, decay parameterization, padding masks, short-history handling, and whether pooling includes the current visible item.",
    "The sampled-softmax objective needs an explicit formula, temperature, treatment of sampling probabilities, and handling of variable negative counts or empty eligible pools. Chunking must preserve the joint softmax denominator.",
    "Recent-item similarity could amplify recently satisfied purchases or broad associations. The report needs a fixed-recency baseline and evidence that the learned gate contributes beyond score scaling. Originality is reasonably rated as incremental; potential and difficulty ratings remain uncertain without these controls and runtime measurements.",
    "No baseline validation HR@10, checkpoint-selection schedule, or concrete GPU-budget allocation is provided. With 200 validation users per category, small gains and repeated checkpoint selection require uncertainty analysis. The required simulator evaluation on twenty training users is also absent from the experimental procedure."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify architectural precedent and identify controls for recency, representation scale, and durable-purchase failure modes.",
      "query": "Sequential recommendation SASRec gated short-term long-term interest fusion recent item embedding pooling: how do FOSSIL, LSIDN, and related methods normalize branches, parameterize recency decay, and ablate learned gates against fixed recent-history fusion?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Make the proposed training objective reproducible and distinguish uncorrected candidate-set cross-entropy from approximations to full-catalog softmax.",
      "query": "Sequential recommendation sampled softmax uniform negatives without replacement user-history exclusion: when are sampling-probability corrections needed, how should variable negative counts be handled, and how can chunked logits preserve an exact cross-entropy denominator?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Assess whether modest validation gains support model selection under the fixed benchmark and limited search budget.",
      "query": "Recommendation evaluation sampled HR@10 with 99 negatives and 200 users per dataset: paired stratified bootstrap confidence intervals, repeated validation checkpoint selection bias, and differences between sampled ranking and full-catalog recommendation quality"
    }
  ]
